{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1137736-technocrats-taking-on-verbena","id":1137736,"title":"Technocrats taking on Verbena","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-05T10:13:28-07:00","id":1137736,"title":"Technocrats taking on Verbena","content":"So my group of Technocrats have decide to go full on Pogrom on some Reality Deviants with Alonson Hardsuits and everything. They're going to be up against some Verbena. I've described them as a Coven of Witches using blood magic. Their goal is to capture the leader and eliminate the rest. What kind of preparations would Verbena have for direct attack by Technocrats? The leader has Arete 4 but I've not settled on anything else yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T10:52:20-07:00","id":1137760,"title":"","content":"Chantry defenses will vary widely depending on the Spheres they have, and the resources they can muster. Countermeasures I imagine for that paradigm may include wards with hexes that activate on intrusion, aggresive plants/animals/insects with uncanny capabilities, a guardian spirit or two. Traditionalist chantries often have a way to flee, that can vary from portals to the umbra to ordinary exits. All of that would be pretty standard...but really it depends a lot on Spheres &amp; resources (quintessence, people, location) they have. Arete 4 could be enough to put some nasty defenses, but not without Spheres, Quint, and help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T11:17:05-07:00","id":1137766,"title":"","content":"If the leader has Forces 4, she can brew up a storm - or more likely heavy cloud cover - in a teapot, which would block satellite access; that might be problematic for your Technocrats. <br /> <br /> Is there a good reason for the witches to stay where they are? (That is, do they have a powerful Node / their world-tree / irreplaceable material possessions there?) If not, Correspondence 4 or Spirit 4 would let them walk the Paths of the Wyck and escape easily.<br /> <br /> You'd definitely have a lot of animated plants/animals. That's probably not a big deal given the hardsuits unless you decide the leader has Life 4 and is creating huge shambling mounds.<br /> <br /> If the witches really hate these guys, they could just Rip the Man-Body with Life 3. Whatever cool tech your PCs have on the outside, they remain flesh and blood on the inside, just like everyone else. It would definitely look like &quot;blood magic&quot; to others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T12:08:18-07:00","id":1137780,"title":"","content":"Yes Life 3 can be pretty deadly...PC can defend against that if they have Primium countermeasures, Life 1 countermagic, or an argumentation that allows them to soak aggravated with their Resistence. If they don't have any of that, the mission may become quite deadly (but who attacks Verbena without some protection against Life?)<br /> <br /> An Idea to depart from the norm: if the witches have Mind/Forces 2-3 (or the leader Mind 4) they could weave potent illusions and use misdirection while they remain hidden, attacking only when/if the chances are on their favor...(like the Bene Gesserit from Duna, your comandos would be attacking a creepy and *empty* chantry with little of value, assailed by doubt and futility)...This can be directly countered with Mind, and other Sphere senses may trigger disbelief, Primium and/or some aplications of Prime also could offer some protection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-05-2017, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T12:16:53-07:00","id":1137784,"title":"","content":"For the leader I was thinking of having Life 4 as her primary sphere. The coven is protecting a Node equivalent to a level 3 Caern that is located on a small island off the coast of Maine, where the story is taking place. I like the idea of it being inaccessible by normal means and using the Paths of the Wyck to get to it. They have plenty of Quintessence and potentially several long running effects going. <br /> <br /> The PCs are rather diverse for a group of Technocrats. There's a representative from every Convention and they each have Enlightment 3 and around 8 dots in Spheres. <br /> <br /> I don't know if they'll go for a full on assault on the Node itself. I think they're smarter than that but I want to be prepared for it just in case. They've already brainstormed ways they can surprise and incapacitate the leader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T12:50:41-07:00","id":1137795,"title":"","content":"Here's a bunch of Fun potential complications: The Node/chantry is in a Primal reality Zone. So just about everything they plan is vulgar. Spirit allies. Bygones since its not a Technocratic Reality Zone.<br /> <br /> Time 4-contingency spells. Correspondence 4-randomly resized and reconnected areas that only people who live there would understand. Diseases/poisons that only work on outsiders because of life/matter tricks.<br /> <br /> <br /> Being completely off the Grid so no Data.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T13:09:05-07:00","id":1137805,"title":"","content":"Indeed, if you play with Reality Zones, since the Chantry it's so isolated it could easily opperate under Verbena Paradigm, lika a big Sanctum, extremely technological effects would be Vulgar, while the Chantry could be filled with all sorts of normaly Vulgar stuff, like chimeras or other mosnters to shoot at (thanks to Life 4).<br /> <br /> If they use the Paths heavily, they may use them to attack or confuse attackers, Portals that open to nasty places if you're not sensing space/dimensions.<br /> <br /> Wards could be placed that affects only non-members with deadly Life 3 &quot;rip the man's body&quot; and/or entropy curses, this goes well with the idea of a secluded cove, You could tie the Wards to the blood of the witches (this would be thematic, I think, but also allow to pass people skillful with Life that can take a blood sample and disguise their Life patterns).<br /> <br /> If they incapacitate the leader, it should be relatively easy to use her knowledge of the Chantry (and it's members) to disable all defenses and take it.<br /> <br /> Of course the leader should have one or two surprises (Like to turn into a swarm of insects or spiders as big as her body to escape, that would be nasty. With a little Mind she could be immune to knock-out and very resistent to effects that would render her unconscious, which may difficult her capture. Artifacts are always useful when in a pinch, and she does have a good amount of Quint, she may have one or two jewels that are more than they appear. Etc, have fun).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T13:22:28-07:00","id":1137810,"title":"","content":"Life 4 allows you to transform yourself and others. Give them hard skin, great wings, sharp claws and the fission of a hawk and an owl rolled into one l.<br /> <br /> As some forces to make them Breath fire, make those determined to fight to the death become full on dragons.<br /> <br /> If they have any Matter magic on them, they could even transform into the elements themselves. Life and Matter for earth, air, and water, forces and life for Fire.<br /> <br /> Also, have them fight smart. They know what they are protecting, they could easily create a show of a big fight to distract them long enough to get the real objective (or at least what they think the PCs are after) long out of harms way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-06-2017, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T14:57:36-07:00","id":1137836,"title":"","content":"I forgot yeah at life four all sorts of fun classical allusions you could get people turned into pigs, newts etc... Since they could have artifacts contingency spells, wards built in they could add all sorts of chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T23:16:30-07:00","id":1137929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1137736-technocrats-taking-on-verbena?p=1137766#post1137766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the leader has Forces 4, she can brew up a storm - or more likely heavy cloud cover - in a teapot, which would block satellite access; that might be problematic for your Technocrats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmh. I doubt a mundane cloud cover would block technocratic sattelites. I even recall them having communications Devices that work under miles of rock.<br /> <br /> That said...I think attacking the Verbena in their wilderness Chantry with Alandson Hardsuits (And a mixed Amalgam no less which is bound to have people not trained in their use..) sounds exceedingly inefficient and haphazard.<br /> Not only are five of those suits an utterly expensive treatment in terms of resources which would require that Coven to have done something *really horrible*, but also fighting on the Verbena's turf is the worst possible scenario and a risk to assets.<br /> <br /> Since the location of the wilderness Node seems to be known, the smarter (and less expensive way in terms of risk and assets) way would be to do satellite surveillance of that spot, tracking the members of the Coven, and doing a more covert strike once the members are in surroundings where they do not have as many advantages - the outskirts of a town for example.<br /> <br /> I am sure the NWO would suggest tracking their daily routines, and then preparing traps in streets individual members often pass though - using Mind procedures to block off the local populance, and then distributing five sniper rifles instead of Alandson Hardsuits.<br /> <br /> Even if this might not take out all Reality Deviants at once,, humans are creatures of habit, and taking out a majority of them at once when they go about their daily (mundane) lives in this manner would be possible, with minimal risk and expenses involved.<br /> <br /> ...if maybe not as fun. Depends. Then again, you could spice things up as it gets revealed that at least one member (or even the Leader) has a high Arcane and cannot be tracked that way...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-06-2017, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T06:07:50-07:00","id":1137996,"title":"","content":"Yeah I don't think they're going to go full on frontal assault, but it doesn't hurt for me to be prepared for that just in case. More likely they're going to target them individually, starting with the leader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T18:50:57-07:00","id":1138174,"title":"","content":"If you want to play up the depth of things the Technocrats don't understand, say that a past mage at the chantry was sacrificed to empower the Node, per the fancy Prime 3 rote the Verbena have, and that his or her presence persists in some way. The witches always know where the invaders are, the PC's minds seem foggy and unfocused, their tech goes on the fritz...<br /> <br /> Plus, if they win and take the Node, they can discover that the witches somehow imprinted a mental resonance on the primal energy flows in the area, and they get to &quot;reformat&quot; the place Ghostbusters style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T20:52:03-07:00","id":1138487,"title":"","content":"That's a pretty thematic and cool idea.<br /> <br /> What about protections that aren't limited to the Node/Chantry? Personal protective measures they might have when they have access to a wealth of Tass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T21:16:01-07:00","id":1138489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1137736-technocrats-taking-on-verbena?p=1138174#post1138174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to play up the depth of things the Technocrats don't understand, say that a past mage at the chantry was sacrificed to empower the Node, per the fancy Prime 3 rote the Verbena have, and that his or her presence persists in some way. The witches always know where the invaders are, the PC's minds seem foggy and unfocused, their tech goes on the fritz...<br /> <br /> Plus, if they win and take the Node, they can discover that the witches somehow imprinted a mental resonance on the primal energy flows in the area, and they get to &amp;quot;reformat&amp;quot; the place Ghostbusters style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe there is some safeguard in place to let the spirit leave or at the very least withhold power from the Node unless the Techs come to terms with it?<br /> <br /> What sort of allies/enemies could the Technocrats be facing? Perhaps the local Sabbat knows where the Chantry is and the Verbena kicks the hornets nest as it were on the way out to make sure that the Technocrats new base is targeted for a mass assault?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}